  "body": "**Stacked on #674** (#669, the plasma machine kind and the 1300PL). Review only this PR's own commit, `3b722b0f`.\n\nA **Plasma Profile** operation and a **plasma torch** tool (#670).\n\n## What changed\n- **Torch tool (`ToolKind::Torch`):**\n  - its diameter is the **kerf width**; rpm and corner radius are 0;\n  - a torch stating an rpm is refused by name at `AddTool`, `ChangeTool` and the library reader;\n  - a catalog `PT-KERF-150` (1.5 mm), with project round-trip.\n  - **Side fix:** the editor's kind list was missing \"Touch probe\", so editing a probe silently turned it into a chamfer mill. It now lists \"Touch probe\" and \"Plasma torch\".\n- **New `OpType::PlasmaProfile` / `Family::Plasma` / `Section::Plasma`:**\n  - appended at stored id 39, so no existing id moves;\n  - plasma ops are allowed only on a plasma table, and the command door refuses both directions by name;\n  - **Behaviour change:** the mill-turn now admits only milling and turning (before, it admitted every family).\n- **`PlasmaOp` parameters:**\n  - clearance, plate top and bottom, an optional kerf override;\n  - compensation in the computer, or G41/G42 at the control;\n  - `reversed`, lead-in and lead-out lengths;\n  - the small-hole diameter (32 mm), feed factor (0.65) and overburn;\n  - optional feed, pierce height, cut height and delay. Blank leaves them to the controller's AutoFS.\n- **Generator (`crates/motion/src/plasma/`).** The provenance cites Hypertherm's direction guidance, the LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §13, and Tormach's 1300PL manual and post guidelines.\n  - **Roles and order:** a ring is a hole if air sits just inside it, and its parent is the smallest closed ring around it. **Everything nested inside is cut before what encloses it** (island → hole → outline).\n  - **Kerf:** offset by kerf/2 to the waste side by default. With G41/G42, a `CompSpan` gets straight entry and exit leads at least the kerf radius long; shorter is refused.\n  - **Direction:** outer contours run CW and holes CCW; `reversed` flips both and is stated.\n  - **Leads:** quarter-arc on the waste side, at mid-longest-edge. With no room a lead is halved up to 4×, with a note, then refused.\n  - **Small holes:** pierced at the centre, a perpendicular lead-in, **no lead-out**, overburn, and feed × factor.\n  - **Kerf law:** every lit move is sampled every 0.25 mm and must keep the kerf off the part, or the op is refused naming the contour.\n  - **Refused by name:** degenerate, self-crossing and pinched contours, kerf ≤ 0, and a hole smaller than the kerf.\n- **Wiring through #674:** `cuts_plasma` recognises the family, so the 1300PL check judges XY travel and feed. The ribbon shows the Plasma section on a plasma table only. The op page is `plasma_page.rs`.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/670-plasma-profile.md`.\n\n## CL records (for #671's post and #672's laws; documented in CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md)\n```\n; PLASMA KERF<µm> [CONTROL] [PIERCE<µm>] [CUTH<µm>] [DELAY<ms>] [AUTOFEED] [REVERSED]\n; TORCH ON C<id> OUTER|INNER|OPEN [PARENT<id>] [SMALL<factor×1000>]\n; TORCH OFF C<id>\n```\n- **Placement:** the PLASMA header comes once, after START. Contour ids run in cut order, and PARENT names the enclosing closed contour.\n- **Parser:** the records are comment lines, so the post-stream parser skips them. The CL reader refuses a missing header, overlapping spans, a rapid inside a span, duplicate ids, a bad parent and an unextinguished torch.\n- **Round-trip:** they survive the CL text dump and the project's path cache.\n\n## How tested\n- **Motion `plasma` (11):**\n  - kerf side, directions and reversal;\n  - leads;\n  - the small-hole rule, including the thickness rule;\n  - island before hole, and a lone hole read as a hole;\n  - refusals;\n  - G41/G42 spans, open runs, and the CL text round-trip.\n- **App `plasma_profile` (7):**\n  - the torch and its rpm refusal;\n  - the family door both ways;\n  - a holed plate with a clean 1300PL check;\n  - a hole smaller than the kerf refused;\n  - create and edit undo/redo;\n  - a picked face equals the whole model;\n  - save and load byte-identical.\n- **Golden:** `plasma_plate_with_holes.cl` (an island in a Ø40 hole, a Ø10 small hole, a slot).\n- **UI:** the op shows on a plasma ribbon only, and the editor round-trips a torch.\n- **Gate:**\n  - every camcraft-app, sim and post test binary passes, as do the motion, cl and tools suites;\n  - ui lib 378 pass. The 1 failure is the known no-GPU test;\n  - clippy is clean on 5 crates. No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\n## Not judged here (for #672)\n- Slots or inlets on an outer contour narrower than the kerf.\n- Kerf crossings between contours, and tip-up.\n- A path whose plasma record fails on load loses it, so #671's post must refuse a Plasma Profile path without one.\n\nChangelog: A Plasma Profile operation and a plasma torch tool (kerf = diameter, no rpm): kerf offset in the computer or G41/G42, outer CW / holes CCW (overridable), arc leads, the small-hole rule, holes cut before their outline, optional feed/pierce/cut height/delay; the CL carries PLASMA / TORCH ON / TORCH OFF records (#670)\n\nFixes #670\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
